WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.989
Tired of the MCU Hulk being kind of a joke?

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:08.029
There's one story from the comics that could
bring out the devil in him.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:12.690
She-Hulk, also known as Jennifer Walters,
has finally arrived in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.520
Universe, and luckily for her, she has a Hulk
to teach her the ropes.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.660
Although the Disney+ series is very much Jennifer's
story, her cousin Bruce Banner is also a key

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.990
part of it — at least to start.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.680
He's the reason she gets her powers following
a car accident.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.250
Not only that, a Sakaaran ship that causes
the crash in the first place, and it's clearly

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.969
looking for the green champion who once fought
on the planet as a gladiator.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:42.129
So Marvel Studios may be gearing up to take
a stab at the full "World War Hulk" storyline.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:44.350
"Sakarran class-A courier craft.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.180
They're probably trying to deliver a message.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.863
I gotta get to the bottom of that."

00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:52.679
The Hulk has become more of a comedic character
of late thanks to Professor Hulk.

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:57.359
An adaptation of "World War Hulk" would help
him get back his dark edge, but another would

00:00:57.359 --> 00:01:02.579
take things even further: writer Al Ewing
and artist Joe Bennett's "Immortal Hulk."

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:08.060
The series not only takes a deep dive into
what makes Bruce Banner tick, but it recontextualizes

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:12.759
the Hulk's powers, his origin, and his place
in the wider Marvel Universe.

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:17.140
The story sees Bruce as a nomad who roams
the United States while trying to keep both

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.630
hands on his mental steering wheel.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:24.539
Ewing and Bennett also hold up a mirror to
the ugliest parts of society, and how the

00:01:24.539 --> 00:01:26.580
Hulk reckons with humanity.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.950
The first issue sees the Hulk hunt down a
man who accidentally kills a 12-year-old girl

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.369
in a gas station robbery gone wrong.

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:36.530
From there, the stories only get darker.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:41.609
It essentially proposes the idea that while
Banner can be killed, the Hulk takes over

00:01:41.609 --> 00:01:44.829
at night, resurrecting him if he has to.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:51.640
It also reveals that the Hulk's worst identity,
Devil Hulk, has become the most dominant personality.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:56.920
While the MCU has acknowledged Banner's trouble
balancing his personalities over the years…

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:57.625
"Come on!

00:01:57.625 --> 00:01:58.688
Come on!"

00:01:59.235 --> 00:02:01.515
"Nooooo!"

00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:07.060
…it has never relished in letting the Hulk
loose.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:13.106
He got to smash bad guys in all the "Avengers"
movies, but it's not the same as having him run wild.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:20.178
And what better way to let him off the chain
than by analyzing his psyche in a dark, intense story?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.580
The only problem with adapting "Immortal Hulk"
is the stunning body horror that Al Ewing

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.360
and Joe Bennett weave throughout their series.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:33.689
It's impressive that Marvel let the duo get
away with some of the grotesque imagery on the page.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.970
For example, there's the infamous moment involving
the Abomination in "Immortal Hulk" #18.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:43.800
Although Hulk assumes that it's Emil Blonsky,
the monster looks different because his head

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.040
looks like a closed fist.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:52.290
It's actually two closed fists, and when they
unfurl, they reveal the two distorted faces

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:57.920
of former Hulk sidekick Rick Jones, who's
been experimented on by a nefarious organization.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.530
It's a truly grim revelation, and it's just
one of many violent designs that pop up over

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.150
the course of the series.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.430
Although the MCU has dabbled in horror with
the likes of the "Doctor Strange" movies,

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:16.623
depicting graphic gamma-induced transformations
and breakdowns might be too far for the House of Mouse.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.430
But with some clever concessions, Marvel Studios
could still bring the story to life.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.950
After all, if Scarlet Witch can ruthlessly
slaughter the Illuminati in "Doctor Strange

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.850
in the Multiverse of Madness," there's a way
of showing the Rick Jones Abomination.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:35.670
MCU head Kevin Feige confirmed at San Diego
Comic-Con 2022 that the current era of the

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:42.010
MCU is titled "The Multiverse Saga," building
toward "Avengers: The Kang Dynasty" and "Avengers:

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.010
Secret Wars."

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:47.240
An "Immortal Hulk" movie could absolutely
fit into that frame.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.850
A huge part of the story revolves around the
idea that there's a terrifying realm that

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.487
lurks at the very bottom of the multiverse.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:56.790
"I'm sorry.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.687
You're saying there's a multiverse?"

00:03:58.687 --> 00:04:00.150
And it's growing!

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:06.863
In "Immortal Hulk," the Below-Place is essentially
hell for anyone who's been transformed by gamma radiation.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:11.900
People who have been there can come back from
the dead, they won't remember their time there.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:17.590
It's ruled by a cruel force called the One
Below All, who is hell-bent on wiping out

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.310
all life in the multiverse.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:25.000
Essentially, this terrifying entity can possess
most gamma-irradiated monsters as a host,

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.310
although the Hulk eventually manages to cut
it off from the rest of the multiverse.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:34.720
So an "Immortal Hulk" movie would introduce
a new realm of existence, just like "Shang-Chi,"

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.640
"Loki," Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of
Madness," and "Thor: Love and Thunder" have.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:44.790
So not only could an "Immortal Hulk" movie
slot perfectly into the current direction

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:50.660
of the MCU, but it would deliver a completely
fresh take on Hulk and Bruce Banner.

